+## 8. Replay set construction & validation (rounds 8–11, 2026-10-12)
+
+`bench/build_replay_set.py` (committed; run as `python3 bench/build_replay_set.py`)
+converts the recorded traffic into
+- `bench/.replay/m1/agent.jsonl`, `mem.jsonl` — gitignored, recorded content
+- `bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/replay_manifest.json` — committed, no recorded
+  content
+
+Final full host run log: `bench/results/2026-10-12/autopilot/replay-set-r10.log`.
+
+**Composition.** 30 agent requests: 3 top-scoring steps per arm (`step_score`
+weights file reads/edits/test output), 5 spread turns each — baseline-r0/0,
+baseline-r1/0, baseline-r1/2, mem0-r0/0, mem0-r1/0, mem0-r2/0 (6 distinct steps).
+12 mem requests from the mem0 arm, 5 distinct steps (mem0-r0/0, mem0-r0/1, mem0-r0/2,
+mem0-r1/0, mem0-r1/1). `n_messages mismatches: 0` on all 30 agent requests —
+rebuilt histories match the recorded tap record counts, so bodies are checked
+against real traffic.
+
+**Bodies.** Agent: messages = rebuilt system prompt + full history before the
+turn; assistant thinking kept as `reasoning_content` (§8.1); tools = the arm's
+pi tool schemas (mem0_memory in the mem0 arm). Mem: system =
+ADDITIVE_EXTRACTION_PROMPT verbatim (33,655 chars, single-pass `\\`/`\``/`\\uXXXX`
+unescape); user = the `generateAdditiveExtractionPrompt` template
+(`mem0_extract_src.txt:1137`): existing = latest 10 live ADD/UPDATE memories
+created before the per-call cutoff (DELETE rows removed via the `action` column;
+not the 10 nearest by embedding); newMessages = `role: content` lines
+(`mem0_extract_src.txt:838`), one new message + one cutoff per call (5 auto-captures
++ 7 tool-adds). Plus `response_format: {type: json_object}` and
+`chat_template_kwargs: {enable_thinking: false}`. No sampling params in any body;
+the probe sets them.
+
+**System prompt.** `system_prompt_exact: true` — rebuilt from the `pi_prompt_src.txt`
+sections, joined by blank lines; the join is *inferred* (`getSystemMessageText`
+not in the dump). Exactness is supported by the n_messages<=3 ratios (6 two-message
+requests): 0.840–0.877.
+
+**Size check (est = prompt_chars/4 vs recorded prompt_n+cache_n).**
+
+| role  | n | prompt chars | recorded tokens | median est/recorded |
+|-------|---|--------------|-----------------|---------------------|
+| agent | 30 | 798,969 | 241,448 | **0.833** |
+| mem   | 12 | 431,077 | 104,716 | **1.027** |
+
+Both medians inside 0.75–1.33 (acceptance). Per-entry: mem entries all 1.02–1.04;
+agent entries 0.742–0.887 (outliers below).
+
+**Reasoning handling.** `chars_by_role["reasoning"]` is 0 on two-message turns and
+non-zero on every long-output turn (baseline-r0/0/5..10: 25,717–26,591 chars;
+mem0-r2/0/8: 19,456; mem0-r0/0/9: 15,440; …) — thinking is captured. On all 30
+agent entries "reasoning after last user only" == "all reasoning": each step is
+a fresh session with the user message before all assistant turns — expected, not
+template evidence. The 0.457 "no reasoning" median (rounds 8–9) confirms recorded
+prompts *did* include earlier reasoning, so pre-fix bodies undersized traffic.
+
+**§8.1 Source confirmation (pi-ai).** pi-ai's converter
+`dist/api/openai-completions.js` (nested under `pi-coding-agent`, i.e. the copy
+pi resolves) confirms the builder assumption at lines 971–999: when no
+`reasoning_details` is present,
+```js
+let signature = nonEmptyThinkingBlocks[0].thinkingSignature;
+if (signature && isOpenAICompletionsReasoningField(signature)) {
+    assistantMsg[signature] = nonEmptyThinkingBlocks
+        .map(block => block.thinking).join("\n");
+}
+```
+i.e. the assistant message goes back under the first thinking block's
+`thinkingSignature` (`reasoning_content` in the recordings) with texts
+newline-joined — exactly what `to_openai()` does. (The `opencode-go` provider
+special-cases `reasoning` → `reasoning_content`; irrelevant for the llama.cpp
+server.)
+
+**Outliers (est/recorded outside 0.75–1.33): 3, all baseline-r0/0.**
+- `inventory-baseline-r0/0/5` 0.740, `0/8` 0.743, `0/10` 0.742.
+
+All three are turns immediately after the longest reasoning outputs in the set
+(25.7k–26.6k chars of reasoning in the prompt). The chars/4 estimator
+*over-counts* tokens for code/JSON-heavy text (tokenizes at <4 chars/token), so
+these reasoning-heavy turns fall just below the 0.75 floor — within 0.3–1.5% of
+it. All other entries are ≥ 0.75 (mem set 1.02–1.04). No estimator change is
+warranted; the probe measures real tok/s regardless of the estimator.
+
+**max_tokens.** Tap records carry only `predicted_n`; `predicted_n == 2048` on
+`inventory-mem0-r0/2/0` indicates a cap was hit (manifest metadata
+`cap_hit_2048`). The replay should reproduce this: the probe should set
+`max_tokens=2048` on that one request (bodies intentionally carry no sampling
+params).
+
+**pi-ai check fix (round 11).** `show_pi_ai_source()` previously printed `[]`
+because it globbed `providers/openai-completions.js`; the resolved copy lives
+under `dist/api/`. It now matches `**/openai-completions.js` across the fnm and
+/opt roots and prefers the nested `pi-coding-agent/node_modules` copy (that's
+what pi resolves). The §8.1 confirmation comes from this check.
